  "root_cause": "Engine-level, not project code: in Godot 4.5.1-stable every Control created and freed leaves 48 bytes of static memory (Panel and Label alike; Node/Node2D/Node3D/raw canvas-item RIDs: 0 B; object count flat). Minimal repro: godot --headless --path . res://tools/profile/control_growth.tscn -- --kind=panel. The step pattern is the engine container doubling. Bisect 21.10: pure domain 60 runs flat (tools/profile/mem_domain.gd); TreeStage and UnitView build/free x120 flat; autoload containers and global signal connections flat (now recorded in each sample as container_bytes / global_connections). Battle UI creates ~750 Controls per battle -> ~36 KB/battle, ~0.2-0.3 MB per full run.",
  "impact": "Negligible for players (a 3-hour session of ~10 runs ~3 MB). Mitigation if ever needed: pool popups/badges/forecast rows instead of recreating them, or a Godot upgrade with the fix. Report upstream with the repro.",
  "memory_static": " Cause found 21.10, see root_cause."
 }
